2.46.m:
Therefore, abandoning all else, one should install the imperishable liṅga;
if it is installed with effort, everything is installed; [if] it is worshipped, [everything] is worshipped.

Thus ends the forty-sixth chapter in the Uttarabhāga of the glorious Liṅgamahāpurāṇa.

2.55.m:
And what is the divine knowledge that bestows liberation, by which creatures are freed?
The holy Lord said:
Mantrayoga is the first, and sparśayoga is the second;
